## 6. Custom validators, ControllerAdvice/ExceptionHandler, interceptors, filters, aspects

Custom validators: none for this path. Telephone E.164 and email validity are enforced by imperative controller code (`toE164`, `normalizeEmail`), not by ConstraintValidators.

`@ControllerAdvice` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` (class line 49-50). It does not transform the request body; it shapes error responses:
- Lines 133-169 `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`: catches Bean Validation failures from item 2/3, returns 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, an `errors` property (list of failing field names) and `schemaValidationErrors` (per-field messages with rejected values).
- Lines 113-124 `handleDataIntegrityViolationException`: maps DB constraint violations to 404.
- Lines 84-87 `handleAccessDeniedException`: re-throws so Spring Security handles 403/entry-point (relevant because of `@PreAuthorize` on the method).
- Lines 96-103 `handleGeneralException`: catch-all -> 500.

Aspects: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CallMonitoringAspect.java` — `@Aspect` (line 38) with `@Around("within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)")` (line 77) that times/counts calls on beans annotated `@Repository`. The Spring Data `SpringDataOwnerRepository` is NOT annotated `@Repository`, so under the default profile this aspect does not wrap the owner save (it applies to the `jpa`/`jdbc` profile repository impls).

Security: the method is guarded by `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` (OwnerRestControllerV1.java line 188), enforced by Spring Security's method interceptor before the body runs. I did not find custom `HandlerInterceptor`/servlet `Filter`/`OncePerRequestFilter` classes in `src` (grep returned none); only the standard Spring Security filter chain applies.

